All 15 Linux-container and 15 TCG runs exit zero. Each source has the same
checksum in all three variants. Every profile reports dropped=0, irregular=0.
Executable load addresses do not overlap init. The existing GCC kernel and
snapshot disk are reused. One CPU and the current QEMU are diagnostic
overrides; these runs do not establish historical kernel acceptance, latency
or all-input equivalence. N08 and N10 remain open; their 2x exits are not met.

Capture: .evidence/live-range-holes-20261016/ (500 MiB limit).
before.json and after.json bind source, compiler, command and assembly.
runtime/counts.json and run-*/result.json bind executable and runtime inputs.
The final compiler differs after rebuilding and the tag-lookup repair;
final.json records byte-identical assembly for all five measured reductions.

Focused allocation and transport tests: 65 PASS. The two new live-segment
tests first failed with the old hull policy. Existing loop and branch tests
then exposed the join-copy naming defect; their failures are retained.
All four changed variadic snapshots match their prior hashes with the old
hull policy on identical EvoIR. Reviewed differences are temporary register
choices and moves, not frame layout, ABI save areas, guards or control edges.

The first original KVM MMU probe reaches the 180-second limit. A diagnostic
repeat finishes in 156.327 seconds; both early samples are in parser tag
lookup, not allocation. That lookup nested a scope-tag scan and a global
binding scan. It now uses the existing per-scope index. A 128/512-tag parser
test changes from 10.839/714.658 ms (RED) to 1.512/5.799 ms (GREEN); separate
tests retain shadowing, forward completion, invalid-scope and rollback rules.
Original units compile and assemble with the final parser: page_alloc in
39.477 s (528,064 object bytes), KVM mmu in 41.902 s (703,544 bytes), and
sha3_generic in 24.846 s (253,720 bytes). The 41 projected Kbuild omissions
per unit are disclosed, with zero unreviewed omissions. This is not exact
argv parity or a kernel boot. Hashed probe intermediates are retired;
commands, source/output hashes, runtime payloads and failed captures remain.

The first full gate has 3,424 passes, three failures and eight ignores.
All failures are proof-required tests: two stale edits changed no byte, and
the pilot expected an old allocation snapshot. Require a nonempty mutation,
retain a stale-edit regression and review the changed output. Three actual
allocation mutants are independently rejected; all 23 corrected tests pass.
Final combined acceptance: 451 suites, 3436 PASS, zero failures and eight
retained ignores; Clippy, formatting and all six Lean gate steps pass.
